\ list-reverse defined a nested list-reverse-acc helper inside its own body,
\ which AOT freeze discovery could not see, so the word failed to compile.
\ Hoisting the helper into a module-scope private{ } block makes cons-list
\ AOT-compilable. Building and reading a cons-list in an AOT binary exercises
\ two freeze->runtime fixes the hoist exposed: the cons variant wraps a
\ cons-cell struct, so its backing struct must survive serialization, and
\ match/head/tail rely on the enum-variant registry being rebuilt at load.
\
\ The conversion words (cons-list>array, list-reverse-acc) recurse inside
\ word-body unchecked-match tables whose arm callees the freeze walk promotes
\ into the must-compile set, so they exercise branch-table promotion under a
\ strict build.

use "cons-list" ;

{ 10 20 30 } >cons-list head .
{ 10 20 30 } >cons-list tail head .
{ 10 20 30 } >cons-list cons? .
nil nil? .
{ 1 2 3 } >cons-list cons-list>array inspect print-line
{ 1 2 3 } >cons-list list-reverse cons-list>array inspect print-line
